# NotebookLM MCP Connectivity Restoration Walkthrough

## Summary
I have successfully restored the configuration for the NotebookLM MCP server in Antigravity. The server is now correctly registered in the application's user profile.

## Changes Made
- **Identified Config Location**: Located the master MCP configuration file at `~/Library/Application Support/Antigravity/User/mcp.json`.
- **Registered Server**: Used the Antigravity CLI ([/Applications/Antigravity.app/Contents/Resources/app/bin/antigravity](file:///Applications/Antigravity.app/Contents/Resources/app/bin/antigravity)) to add the `notebooklm-mcp` definition to the user profile.
- **Config Verification**: Verified that the server is configured to use the global configuration at `~/.notebooklm-mcp/notebooklm-config.json` and the existing authenticated Chrome profile.

## Restoration Details
I executed the following command to re-register the server:
```bash
/Applications/Antigravity.app/Contents/Resources/app/bin/antigravity --add-mcp '{
  "name": "notebooklm-mcp",
  "command": "/Users/Office/.local/bin/notebooklm-mcp",
  "args": ["--config", "/Users/Office/.notebooklm-mcp/notebooklm-config.json"]
}'
```

The success was confirmed by the CLI output and the presence of the configuration in:
[mcp.json](file:///Users/Office/Library/Application Support/Antigravity/User/mcp.json)

## Next Steps
> [!IMPORTANT]
> To fully enable the tools in this chat session, you may need to **restart Antigravity**. Once restarted, I will have direct access to the `notebooklm-mcp` tools (such as `chat`, `test`, and `list_notebooks`).

## Proof of Work
The configuration is now correctly persisted:
```json
{
        "servers": {
                "notebooklm-mcp": {
                        "command": "/Users/Office/.local/bin/notebooklm-mcp",
                        "args": [
                                "--config",
                                "/Users/Office/.notebooklm-mcp/notebooklm-config.json"
                        ]
                }
        }
}
```
